Third-party components
----------------------

The NOMAD DLL embeds ONNX Runtime 1.31.0 (Microsoft, MIT), its supplied third-party
notices, and the YOLOX Nano COCO model from Megvii-BaseDetection/YOLOX 0.1.1rc0
(Apache-2.0). The unmodified model SHA256 is
c789161ed43c8269fcd4e67c67eeeb4e80c622da2eb296a20bc6007bd18a0b7d.
Pinned source URLs and archive/file checksums are in scripts/build/prepare_vision.ps1.
ONNX Runtime source revision: 402979ac1bef89dcd55add41eaa7277c407599eb.
The embedded NOMAD.Vision.ONNX-RUNTIME-LICENSE.txt, ONNX-RUNTIME-NOTICES.txt and
YOLOX-LICENSE.txt resources retain the complete upstream licenses and notices;
the plugin extracts them beside its owned per-user runtime cache when vision starts.
Upstream projects: https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime and
https://github.com/Megvii-BaseDetection/YOLOX.

Region tracking additionally embeds OpenCvSharp4 4.10.0.20241108 and its Windows
x64 OpenCvSharpExtern library (OpenCV 4.10.0). OpenCvSharp/OpenCV use Apache-2.0;
the native library includes separately licensed third-party components and Intel
IPP. Complete upstream notices and the Intel IPP EULA are retained in
mission_planner/third_party and embedded as NOMAD.Vision.OpenCvSharp-NOTICES.txt
and NOMAD.Vision.OPENCV-IPP-EULA.rtf, extracted beside the owned tracker cache.
This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.
No FFmpeg DLL is included in the NOMAD artifact.

Mission Planner and its installed dependencies are supplied by the host installation,
not bundled into the NOMAD DLL artifact. Retain their applicable notices when
redistributing any such software separately.

The optional ArduPilot firmware patch is a separate GPL-licensed component in
firmware/ardupilot. Its upstream notice and complete corresponding source must
accompany firmware delivery. It is not linked into the NOMAD plugin DLL.

